.TH "VINPUT\-CONFIG" "5" "September 2026" "fcitx5\-vinput" "fcitx5\-vinput File Formats"
.SH NAME
vinput\-config \- Configuration format and options for fcitx5\-vinput
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]fcitx5\-vinput\f[R] uses two configuration files:
.IP "1." 3
\f[I]\(ti/.config/vinput/config.json\f[R] \(em Core configuration for
audio capture, ASR engines, LLM providers, and postprocessing scenes.
.IP "2." 3
\f[I]\(ti/.config/fcitx5/conf/vinput.conf\f[R] \(em Fcitx5 addon
configuration for keybindings and UI settings.
.SH CONFIG.JSON STRUCTURE
The core configuration file is JSON\-formatted with four top\-level
sections: \f[B]global\f[R], \f[B]asr\f[R], \f[B]llm\f[R], and
\f[B]scenes\f[R].
.SS GLOBAL SECTION
Controls runtime audio environment and capture settings.
.IP
.EX
\(dqglobal\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] {
  \(dqdefault_language\(dq: \(dqen\(dq,
  \(dqcapture_device\(dq: \(dqdefault\(dq,
  \(dqduck_output_while_recording\(dq: \f[B]false\f[R],
  \(dqduck_output_volume\(dq: 0.25
}
.EE
.TP
\f[B]default_language\f[R] (\f[I]string\f[R])
Default UI/model language code (e.g.
\f[CR]\(dqen\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqzh\(dq\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]capture_device\f[R] (\f[I]string\f[R])
PipeWire capture node name, or \f[CR]\(dqdefault\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]duck_output_while_recording\f[R] (\f[I]boolean\f[R])
Whether to lower system audio volume via WirePlumber while recording.
.TP
\f[B]duck_output_volume\f[R] (\f[I]float\f[R], \f[CR]0.0\f[R] \- \f[CR]1.0\f[R])
Target volume fraction when ducking is active (\f[CR]0.25\f[R] = 25%
original volume).
.SS ASR SECTION
Configures offline and cloud speech recognition engines.
.IP
.EX
\(dqasr\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] {
  \(dqactive_provider\(dq: \(dqsherpa\-onnx\(dq,
  \(dqnormalize_audio\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R],
  \(dqinput_gain\(dq: 1.0,
  \(dqvad\(dq: {
    \(dqenabled\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R],
    \(dqthreshold\(dq: 0.5,
    \(dqmin_speech_duration\(dq: 0.15,
    \(dqspeech_pad_ms\(dq: 300
  },
  \(dqproviders\(dq: [ \f[B]...\f[R] ]
}
.EE
.TP
\f[B]active_provider\f[R] (\f[I]string\f[R])
ID of the active ASR provider.
Use \f[CR]\(dqsherpa\-onnx\(dq\f[R] for the offline local engine.
.TP
\f[B]normalize_audio\f[R] (\f[I]boolean\f[R])
Normalize input audio waveforms before recognition.
.TP
\f[B]input_gain\f[R] (\f[I]float\f[R])
Software recording volume multiplier.
.TP
\f[B]vad.enabled\f[R] (\f[I]boolean\f[R])
Enable Voice Activity Detection to drop leading and trailing silence.
.SS LLM SECTION
Defines OpenAI\-compatible API endpoints.
.IP
.EX
\(dqllm\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] {
  \(dqproviders\(dq: [
    {
      \(dqid\(dq: \(dqgroq\(dq,
      \(dqbase_url\(dq: \(dqhttps://api.groq.com/openai/v1\(dq,
      \(dqapi_key\(dq: \(dqYOUR_API_KEY\(dq,
      \(dqextra_body\(dq: {}
    }
  ],
  \(dqadapters\(dq: [
    {
      \(dqid\(dq: \(dqmy\-adapter\(dq,
      \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dqpython3\(dq,
      \(dqargs\(dq: [\(dq/path/to/entry.py\(dq],
      \(dqauto_start\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R]
    }
  ]
}
.EE
.TP
\f[B]adapters[].auto_start\f[R] (\f[I]boolean\f[R])
Whether to automatically launch the adapter process when
\f[B]vinput\-daemon\f[R] starts.
.SS SCENES SECTION
Defines prompt templates and candidate counts for text rewriting.
.IP
.EX
\(dqscenes\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] {
  \(dqactive_scene\(dq: \(dq__raw__\(dq,
  \(dqdefinitions\(dq: [
    {
      \(dqid\(dq: \(dq__raw__\(dq,
      \(dqcount\(dq: 0
    },
    {
      \(dqid\(dq: \(dqdefault\(dq,
      \(dqlabel\(dq: \(dqDefault Polish\(dq,
      \(dqprompt\(dq: \(dqFix spelling and punctuation while keeping original meaning.\(dq,
      \(dqprovider_id\(dq: \(dqgroq\(dq,
      \(dqmodel\(dq: \(dqllama\-3.3\-70b\-versatile\(dq,
      \(dqcontext_lines\(dq: 3,
      \(dqcount\(dq: 5
    }
  ]
}
.EE
.TP
\f[B]active_scene\f[R] (\f[I]string\f[R])
ID of the currently selected scene.
\f[CR]__raw__\f[R] skips LLM post\-processing.
.TP
\f[B]context_lines\f[R] (\f[I]integer\f[R])
Number of preceding input lines sent to the LLM as conversational
context.
.TP
\f[B]count\f[R] (\f[I]integer\f[R], \f[CR]0\f[R] \- \f[CR]9\f[R])
Maximum LLM candidate count.
Maximum number of rewritten candidates requested from the LLM (set to
\f[CR]0\f[R] to disable LLM for this scene).
Candidates are deduplicated with the raw ASR transcript.
If only 1 distinct candidate remains, it commits directly to screen; if
distinct choices exist, a candidate menu is shown defaulting to option 1
(the raw ASR transcript when \f[CR]raw_cand\f[R] is true, followed by
rewrite candidates).
.TP
\f[B]raw_cand\f[R] (\f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]true\f[R])
Whether to include the raw speech transcript in candidate options.
When disabled (\f[CR]false\f[R]), the candidate choices only contain
LLM/adapter rewrites, committing directly if only 1 result exists
(compatible with legacy \f[CR]show_raw\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]raw_prev\f[R] (\f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]true\f[R])
Whether to preview the raw transcript in the floating panel during
postprocessing and allow pressing Enter to use it immediately.
When disabled (\f[CR]false\f[R]), postprocessing remains as a compact
single line without expanding the lower transcript box, eliminating
visual flicker for fast local adapters.
.SH VINPUT.CONF STRUCTURE (FCITX5 ADDON)
The Fcitx5 addon configuration file is stored in INI format at
\f[I]\(ti/.config/fcitx5/conf/vinput.conf\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B][Trigger]\f[R]
TriggerMode=Both
TriggerKey=Alt_R
CommandKeys=Control_R
MenuKey=Shift_R
PagePrevKeys=Page_Up,KP_Page_Up
PageNextKeys=Page_Down,KP_Page_Down
MaxStreamingDisplayWidth=60
.EE
.TP
\f[B]TriggerMode\f[R] (\f[I]enum: Tap, Hold, Both\f[R])
Trigger activation mode.
\f[CR]Tap\f[R] toggles recording; \f[CR]Hold\f[R] records while key is
pressed; \f[CR]Both\f[R] enables tap\-to\-toggle and hold\-to\-talk.
.TP
\f[B]TriggerKey\f[R] (\f[I]key list\f[R])
Keys used to trigger voice recording (default: Right Alt).
.TP
\f[B]CommandKeys\f[R] (\f[I]key list\f[R])
Keys used to record a voice command on selected text (default: Right
Control).
.TP
\f[B]MenuKey\f[R] (\f[I]key list\f[R])
Keys used to open the unified command palette (default: Right Shift).
This replaces the old \f[CR]SceneMenuKey\f[R]; \f[CR]AsrMenuKey\f[R] was
removed.
.TP
\f[B]MaxStreamingDisplayWidth\f[R] (\f[I]integer\f[R], \f[CR]0\f[R] \- \f[CR]500\f[R])
Maximum visual column width for live streaming recognition preview.
Older text is folded into \(aqhead...tail\(aq to keep the preedit
tooltip within bounds.
Set to \f[CR]0\f[R] to disable folding (default: \f[CR]60\f[R]).
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]\(ti/.config/vinput/config.json\f[R]
User core configuration file.
.TP
\f[I]\(ti/.config/fcitx5/conf/vinput.conf\f[R]
User Fcitx5 addon configuration file.
.TP
\f[I]\(ti/.var/app/org.fcitx.Fcitx5/config/vinput/config.json\f[R]
Configuration path when running inside Flatpak.
